WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.700
If an attacker wanted our company,
would they start with you?

00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:06.170
The board is the target, by four routes.

00:00:07.583 --> 00:00:08.453
First, home.

00:00:08.778 --> 00:00:12.868
Your work laptop is protected
with multi-factor authentication.

00:00:13.258 --> 00:00:16.568
Your private email,
phone and family tablet are not.

00:00:16.918 --> 00:00:21.378
The UK NCSC calls people in your
position high-risk individuals,

00:00:21.378 --> 00:00:26.228
and says attackers prefer personal
accounts because they are easier.

00:00:26.578 --> 00:00:27.968
Two free settings help:

00:00:28.398 --> 00:00:32.228
the strongest email protection,
and Lockdown Mode on an iPhone.

00:00:33.550 --> 00:00:35.940
Second, your voice and face are public.

00:00:36.255 --> 00:00:39.625
Every keynote and podcast
gives a few minutes of audio.

00:00:39.880 --> 00:00:41.710
In January 2024,

00:00:42.020 --> 00:00:45.460
an engineering firm's
employee in Hong Kong paid

00:00:45.460 --> 00:00:49.370
HK$200 million after a video call.

00:00:49.585 --> 00:00:51.895
Every other participant was a deepfake.

00:00:52.215 --> 00:00:53.565
No system was hacked.

00:00:53.885 --> 00:00:55.455
Only authority was used.

00:00:56.550 --> 00:00:57.920
Third, the board pack.

00:00:58.260 --> 00:01:02.330
One PDF, sent to ten people every month,
holds strategy,

00:01:02.560 --> 00:01:04.250
results and legal disputes.

00:01:04.630 --> 00:01:06.640
The leak rarely comes from the portal.

00:01:07.005 --> 00:01:09.695
It comes from the copy
forwarded to a private mailbox,

00:01:10.305 --> 00:01:13.735
printed for the train,
or opened on the family tablet.

00:01:14.140 --> 00:01:15.230
With personal data,

00:01:15.640 --> 00:01:18.830
a stolen pack can mean
a 72-hour notification.

00:01:20.017 --> 00:01:21.067
Fourth, the road.

00:01:21.427 --> 00:01:25.697
On a trip, the phone is the company:
mail, the board pack and banking.

00:01:26.077 --> 00:01:27.727
At a border it can be inspected.

00:01:28.142 --> 00:01:30.832
In a hotel, the safe is opened by staff.

00:01:31.167 --> 00:01:36.687
The AIVD advises a temporary phone and
laptop for countries with an espionage

00:01:36.687 --> 00:01:37.837
risk.

00:01:38.783 --> 00:01:39.993
What good looks like.

00:01:40.278 --> 00:01:43.908
Strongest protection on private mail,
set up by the company.

00:01:44.188 --> 00:01:48.658
A call-back rule: no payment or bank
change on a call or video alone.

00:01:49.013 --> 00:01:52.343
The board pack is read in the portal,
on a managed device.

00:01:52.688 --> 00:01:56.238
A travel kit, with a loaner
device for high-risk countries.

00:01:56.598 --> 00:02:00.948
The UK NCSC has written guidance
for high-risk individuals.

00:02:02.797 --> 00:02:04.007
A suggested first step.

00:02:04.292 --> 00:02:09.142
Ask the company to set up the strongest
email protection for each household.

00:02:09.417 --> 00:02:10.707
Then agree one rule:

00:02:11.097 --> 00:02:13.627
call back on a known number
before any money moves.

00:02:15.183 --> 00:02:17.513
You are the target, not only the company.

00:02:17.843 --> 00:02:20.973
Most routes close with a setting,
a rule or a kit.

